Description: binutils/testsuite: don't tail the same input and output file
 dejagnu's local_exec opens the output file for writing before the child
 command runs.  When the command reads and writes the very same file
 ("tail -n +4 objdump.out" redirected into objdump.out), the reader can
 see a file that has already been truncated, so the tail output is lost.
 The -Wi test then fails its "file size" check, reports UNTESTED instead
 of PASS and returns early, skipping every later test in objdump.exp.
 Which side of the race wins differs between two builds of identical
 source, so the test logs shipped in binutils-dev (and the test-summary
 used by the regression check) are not reproducible.
 .
 Write the tail output to a separate file instead, as upstream did in
 binutils-gdb commit 71320db6509e.  That commit targets a newer testsuite
 where the temporary file already lives in tmpdir/; here the 2.41 testsuite
 still uses objdump.out in the current directory, so only the output name
 is changed.
Author: Clément Chigot <chigot@adacore.com>
Origin: https://sourceware.org/git/gitweb.cgi?p=binutils-gdb.git;h=71320db6509e0893607e9343b5af56a8c130a2ed
Last-Update: 2026-10-29
---
diff --git a/binutils/testsuite/binutils-all/objdump.exp b/binutils/testsuite/binutils-all/objdump.exp
index 28a7ad67..9315a068 100644
--- a/binutils/testsuite/binutils-all/objdump.exp
+++ b/binutils/testsuite/binutils-all/objdump.exp
@@ -560,8 +560,8 @@ if { ![is_elf_format] } then {
        send_log "\n"
     }
 
-    set got [remote_exec host "tail -n +4 objdump.out" "" "/dev/null" "objdump.out"]
-    set output [remote_upload host objdump.out]
+    set got [remote_exec host "tail -n +4 objdump.out" "" "/dev/null" "objdump.tail"]
+    set output [remote_upload host objdump.tail]
 
     if ![file size $output] then {
        # If the output file is empty, then this target does not
@@ -571,7 +571,7 @@ if { ![is_elf_format] } then {
        return
     }
 
-    if { [regexp_diff objdump.out $srcdir/$subdir/dw5-op.W] } then {
+    if { [regexp_diff objdump.tail $srcdir/$subdir/dw5-op.W] } then {
        fail "objdump -Wi for DW_OP_*"
     } else {
        pass "objdump -Wi for DW_OP_*"
